    "1.0.14": {
      "date": "2026-07-09",
      "components": {
        "c4":             { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/c4",             "lang": "go",     "build": "cmd/c4" },
        "c4sh":           { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/c4sh",           "lang": "go",     "build": "." },
        "c4git":          { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/c4git",          "lang": "go",     "build": "cmd/c4git" },
        "c4py":           { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/c4py",           "lang": "python", "publish": "pypi" },
        "c4ts":           { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/c4ts",           "lang": "typescript", "publish": "npm" },
        "c4-swift":       { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/c4-swift",       "lang": "swift",  "publish": "spm" },
        "libc4":          { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/libc4",          "lang": "c",      "publish": "source" },
        "c4-containers":  { "version": "1.0.14", "repo": "Avalanche-io/c4-containers",  "lang": "docker", "publish": "ghcr" }
      },
      "notes": "Correctness/safety/perf patch. CRITICAL: c4m files produced by guided scans (c4 id --continue) on ≤1.0.13 have wrong directory IDs (the empty-input ID was written for every directory entry) and should be regenerated; file IDs were unaffected. Directory C4 IDs are now computed bottom-up, which also fixes O(2^depth) deep-tree scans (~93s → ~0.007s at depth 20). c4m.Diff keys entries by full path. Null timestamps render as - in structure mode. Safety defaults: c4 patch reconcile forms capture the destination's pre-state durably before applying and print a verbatim revert command; protected-path support closes a data-loss hazard (an unguarded patch could delete .git); snapshots are self-capturing (c4 cat <id> reproduces the manifest from the store alone). Performance: snapshot ingest ~180s → ~4.3s and materialize ~171s → ~4.4s on a 20k-file/105MB tree via the batch durability barrier — now the only durability behavior; the --no-fsync/--durable flags are removed. c4 gc (never released) was withdrawn before shipping. Only c4 has substantive changes; other components ship version-lockstep."
    },
